        "step_anchor": "step-5",
        "title": "Properties of Matrix Addition and Subtraction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Since addition and subtraction of matrices are performed elementwise, they have the same properties as addition and subtraction of real numbers.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Since addition and subtraction of matrices are performed elementwise, they have the same properties as addition and subtraction of real numbers.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, if <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A,]</span> <span class=\"math\">[MATH: B,]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: C]</span> are three <span class=\"math\">[MATH: m \\times n]</span> matrices then we can add them in any order:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: (A+B)+C = A+(B+C) = A+B+C]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, if [MATH: A,] [MATH: B,] and [MATH: C] are three [MATH: m \\times n] matrices then we can add them in any order:\n[MATH: (A+B)+C = A+(B+C) = A+B+C]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Moreover, we can distribute a subtraction over matrices in parentheses:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: A - (B + C) = A - B - C]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Moreover, we can distribute a subtraction over matrices in parentheses:\n[MATH: A - (B + C) = A - B - C]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nSince addition and subtraction of matrices are performed elementwise, they have the same properties as addition and subtraction of real numbers.\n\nContent:\nFor example, if [MATH: A,] [MATH: B,] and [MATH: C] are three [MATH: m \\times n] matrices then we can add them in any order:\n[MATH: (A+B)+C = A+(B+C) = A+B+C]\n\nContent:\nMoreover, we can distribute a subtraction over matrices in parentheses:\n[MATH: A - (B + C) = A - B - C]"
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 6,
        "step_index": 4,
        "item_type": "step",
        "step_type": "example",
        "step_id": "464517",
        "content_id": "4379",
        "dom_id": "step-464517",
