        "title": "Calculating the Sum or Difference of Three or More Matrices Using Distributivity",
        "key_prerequisites": [
          {
            "topic_id": "137",
            "name": "Distributing the Negative Sign in a Linear Expression",
            "href": "/topics/137",
            "type": ""
          }
        ],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A+C-(B+A),]</span> if</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: [1|\u2212 2; sqrt(2)|0; 0|\u2212 2]]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Find [MATH: A+C-(B+A),] if\n\n[MATH: [1|\u2212 2; sqrt(2)|0; 0|\u2212 2]]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses: \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: A + C \u2212 (B + A)|= A + C \u2212 B \u2212 A; = A + C \u2212 B \u2212 A; = C \u2212 B]</span></p><p>We are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: C \u2212 B|= [3|\u2212 1; 1|2; \u2212 6|1] \u2212 [3|\u2212 1; 2|0; \u2212 4|1]; = [3 \u2212 3|\u2212 1 \u2212 (\u2212 1); 1 \u2212 2|2 \u2212 0; \u2212 6 \u2212 (\u2212 4)|1 \u2212 1]; = [0|0; \u2212 1|2; \u2212 2|0]]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n[MATH: A + C \u2212 (B + A)|= A + C \u2212 B \u2212 A; = A + C \u2212 B \u2212 A; = C \u2212 B]\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n[MATH: C \u2212 B|= [3|\u2212 1; 1|2; \u2212 6|1] \u2212 [3|\u2212 1; 2|0; \u2212 4|1]; = [3 \u2212 3|\u2212 1 \u2212 (\u2212 1); 1 \u2212 2|2 \u2212 0; \u2212 6 \u2212 (\u2212 4)|1 \u2212 1]; = [0|0; \u2212 1|2; \u2212 2|0]]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
