        "readable_text": "Prompt:\nFind [MATH: (A + B) \u2212 C \u2212 (B \u2212 C)], if\n\n[MATH: A = [6|7; 4|5], B = [3|2; 2|3], C = [5|1; 6|8].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [0|0; 0|0]]\nb. [MATH: [3|2; 2|3]]\nc. [MATH: [5|7; 7|5]]\nd. [MATH: [6|7; 4|5]]\ne. [MATH: [5|1; 6|8]]"
      }
    ],
    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nIf we want to add (or subtract) three or more matrices, all operations should be done elementwise. For example, suppose\n\nContent:\n[MATH: [1; 1; \u2212 1]]\n\nContent:\nThen we can calculate [MATH: {A}+{B}-{C}] by performing the operations on each corresponding entry, as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: A + B \u2212 C|= [1; 1; \u2212 1] + [\u2212 1; 2; 0] \u2212 [0; 5; \u2212 2]; = [1 + (\u2212 1) \u2212 0; 1 + 2 \u2212 5; \u2212 1 + 0 \u2212 (\u2212 2)]; = [0; \u2212 2; 1]]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Calculating the Sum or Difference of Three or More Matrices\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: A-(B-C),] where\n\n[MATH: [\u2212 1|0; 2|\u2212 2]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nPerforming the operations on each corresponding entry, we get:\n\n[MATH: A \u2212 (B \u2212 C)|= [\u2212 1|0; 2|\u2212 2] \u2212 ([\u2212 1|\u2212 1; 2|0] \u2212 [0|\u2212 5; 1|1]); = [\u2212 1|0; 2|\u2212 2] \u2212 [\u2212 1 \u2212 0|\u2212 1 \u2212 (\u2212 5); 2 \u2212 1|0 \u2212 1]; = [\u2212 1|0; 2|\u2212 2] \u2212 [\u2212 1|4; 1|\u2212 1]; = [\u2212 1 \u2212 (\u2212 1)|0 \u2212 4; 2 \u2212 1|\u2212 2 \u2212 (\u2212 1)]; = [0|\u2212 4; 1|\u2212 1]]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: A + B + C], where\n[MATH: A = [1|3; 3|1], B = [4|1; 1|4], C = [\u2212 1|1; 1|\u2212 1].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [5|4; 4|5]]\nb. [MATH: [5|5; 5|4]]\nc. [MATH: [4|5; 4|4]]\nd. [MATH: [4|5; 5|4]]\ne. [MATH: [4|4; 5|4]]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: D \u2212 (E \u2212 F)], where\n[MATH: D = [7|4; 3|5], E = [2|2; 1|4], F = [1|0; 0|2].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [5|5; 2|3]]\nb. [MATH: [6|5; 3|3]]\nc. [MATH: [6|5; 2|2]]\nd. [MATH: [6|4; 2|3]]\ne. [MATH: [6|2; 2|3]]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Tutorial: Properties of Matrix Addition and Subtraction\n\nContent:\nSince addition and subtraction of matrices are performed elementwise, they have the same properties as addition and subtraction of real numbers.\n\nContent:\nFor example, if [MATH: A,] [MATH: B,] and [MATH: C] are three [MATH: m \\times n] matrices then we can add them in any order:\n[MATH: (A+B)+C = A+(B+C) = A+B+C]\n\nContent:\nMoreover, we can distribute a subtraction over matrices in parentheses:\n[MATH: A - (B + C) = A - B - C]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Calculating the Sum or Difference of Three or More Matrices Using Distributivity\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind [MATH: A+C-(B+A),] if\n\n[MATH: [1|\u2212 2; sqrt(2)|0; 0|\u2212 2]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n[MATH: A + C \u2212 (B + A)|= A + C \u2212 B \u2212 A; = A + C \u2212 B \u2212 A; = C \u2212 B]\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n[MATH: C \u2212 B|= [3|\u2212 1; 1|2; \u2212 6|1] \u2212 [3|\u2212 1; 2|0; \u2212 4|1]; = [3 \u2212 3|\u2212 1 \u2212 (\u2212 1); 1 \u2212 2|2 \u2212 0; \u2212 6 \u2212 (\u2212 4)|1 \u2212 1]; = [0|0; \u2212 1|2; \u2212 2|0]]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nFind [MATH: Q + R \u2212 (Q + P)], if\n\n[MATH: P = [3|4; 2|1], Q = [6|7; 2|3], R = [5|6; 6|7].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [2|2; 4|5]]\nb. [MATH: [2|2; 3|6]]\nc. [MATH: [2|1; 4|6]]\nd. [MATH: [1|2; 4|6]]\ne. [MATH: [2|2; 4|6]]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nFind [MATH: (A + B) \u2212 C \u2212 (B \u2212 C)], if\n\n[MATH: A = [6|7; 4|5], B = [3|2; 2|3], C = [5|1; 6|8].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [0|0; 0|0]]\nb. [MATH: [3|2; 2|3]]\nc. [MATH: [5|7; 7|5]]\nd. [MATH: [6|7; 4|5]]\ne. [MATH: [5|1; 6|8]]"
